agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/claude-fable.md:11:**3. The banner treats "never connected" as "expired."** The design branches on `SchwabToken.usable?`, which is false with no row at all. First login shows "Token expired. Sync paused. Re-authenticate," and `Sync::TickJob#pause!` has already written a pause reason that says "re-authenticate" (app/jobs/sync/tick_job.rb:49). Revoked is a third distinct case: Schwab rejected the refresh, and the copy should say so with `last_refresh_error`. `Schwab::TokenHealthJob#nag_reason` already has the right taxonomy, missing, revoked, expired, missed_sunday, expiring (app/jobs/schwab/token_health_job.rb:17-24), but it is private to the job. Extract it to `SchwabToken.status` and use it in the banner, the system page, the mailer, and `get_account_health` in step 8. That is the single method step 7 most needs and does not have.
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/claude-fable.md:53:| `SchwabToken.status` extracted from the health job | `SchwabToken`, `TokenHealthJob` | Item 3; one taxonomy for banner, system page, mailer, MCP |
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-review-build-st/claude-fable.md:1:Review complete. Findings below, ordered by severity, with the sequence walk, spec gaps, and the status of the earlier concerns at the end.
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.stderr:53:- Playwright via a test-only `/playwright/scenarios/:name` reseed route: healthy, expiring, expired, halted, MCP 401 page (step 8), re-auth success and failure, trade review flow.
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.stderr:285:A personal investment operating system for a Schwab taxable brokerage account. A Rails application acts as the system of record and the sole gateway to Schwab's Trader API. Claude acts as the analysis and workflow agent on top of it, via an MCP server the Rails app exposes. The human approves every order.
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.stderr:308:┌─────────────┐     MCP (tools)      ┌──────────────────────────┐
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.stderr:327:**Why an MCP server and not the agent hitting Schwab directly:** one credential holder, one audit log, one place guardrails run. The MCP tool surface is the contract.
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.stderr:380:Hard rule: guardrails are enforced in Rails. The agent can read them and reason about them; it cannot bypass or edit them through MCP.
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.stderr:415:### 5.5 MCP Tool Surface (agent-facing)
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.stderr:429:Explicitly absent from MCP: submit_order, cancel_order, edit_risk_rules, token operations. Submission happens only in the Rails approval UI (or a signed confirmation link), by the human.
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.stderr:435:- **Interactive (human present):** the Claude app (desktop/Cowork/web) with the Rails MCP server registered as a remote connector. Rails exposes MCP over HTTPS with bearer-token auth (token in dokku config, rotatable). This is where ad hoc analysis, screening, and order proposals happen, billed through the Claude subscription seat.
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.stderr:436:- **Scheduled (unattended):** Solid Queue jobs on the VPS call the Anthropic Messages API directly with an API key, passing tool definitions that map to the same internal service layer the MCP server uses (in-process, no MCP hop). Output is rendered to email. This covers the 07:00 brief, 16:30 EOD, and Sunday review. **Unattended runs get read-only tools only.** These runs ingest untrusted text (transcripts, news, fetched pages), so `propose_order`, `add_watchlist_item`, and `annotate_trade` are not in their tool set; anything a brief wants to suggest is rendered as text in the email, and the human creates the proposal interactively. Write tools exist only in the interactive runtime. Each scheduled job also has a hard cap on tool turns. Rationale: unattended runs can't depend on a desktop app being open, and keeping the scheduler in Rails means the VPS is the single ops surface (one place for cron, retries, failure alerts, and the token-health gate).
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.stderr:440:One tool surface, two transports: the MCP server (remote, for the app) and the API tool definitions (in-process, for jobs) both delegate to the same service objects, so guardrails and read models cannot diverge between runtimes.
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.stderr:448:- Repo is git-versioned with one writer: John. Rails never commits to it. Generated context (setup stats, edge summary) is served through the `get_setup_stats` MCP tool and injected into scheduled-run prompts at runtime, so `edge.md` stays a human-authored narrative and there is no second writer to conflict with. The VPS pulls the repo on a schedule (or post-receive hook) for the agent's read access.
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.stderr:475:- **Auth to the Rails app:** the native shell holds a session like the browser does; no separate API auth. The MCP bearer token is never on the phone.
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.stderr:527:**Phase 1 (read-only):** Schwab OAuth + token lifecycle, account/position/transaction sync, dashboard, journal auto-population from fills, memory repo, MCP read tools, daily briefs.
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.stderr:528:**Phase 2 (propose + approve):** guardrail engine, order proposals via MCP, approval UI, bracket submission (entry + child stop, 5.4.2) from UI, ambiguous-outcome reconciliation, settlement checks from broker balances, wash-sale checks against the linked IRA, Hotwire Native iOS app with push and Face ID confirm (5.8a). Ships with shadow mode on.
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.stderr:551:1. **Secrets in Rails credentials**, production-only file (`config/credentials/production.yml.enc`), keys `schwab.app_key`, `schwab.app_secret`, `mcp.bearer_token`, `anthropic.api_key`, `resend.api_key`, plus Active Record Encryption keys. `SCHWAB_CALLBACK_URL` and `MEMORY_REPO_PATH` stay in dokku ENV (not secret). The dokku `SCHWAB_APP_KEY`/`SCHWAB_APP_SECRET` vars get unset once the credentials file is on the server. Rotating the MCP token is an edit to the credentials file plus a deploy.
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.stderr:558:8. **MCP auth (open verification, not blocking):** the Claude app's custom-connector UI exposes static bearer headers only to orgs in a beta. John checks Settings → Connectors → Add custom connector for a "headers" option before step 8. If absent, the fallback is a minimal OAuth 2.1 authorization-code + PKCE endpoint on the app that issues the same bearer after magic-link login. `McpAuth` verifies the bearer either way, so the tool layer is unaffected.
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.stderr:587:| 20 | `tool_calls` | `agent_run_id` (nullable), `transport` enum (mcp, scheduled), `tool_name`, `arguments` jsonb, `duration_ms`, `error`, `created_at`. This is where MCP and runtime tool telemetry goes, not `audit_events`. | yes |
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.stderr:640:`app/models/agent/tools/*` each defines `name`, `description`, `input_schema`, `call(**args)`, and permission metadata: `read_only`, `interactive_allowed`, `scheduled_allowed`. The MCP server registers tools where `interactive_allowed`; the scheduled runtime passes only tools where `scheduled_allowed && read_only`, enforced in one place so a Phase 2 write tool cannot reach an unattended run by omission. Phase 1 tools:
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.stderr:654:**MCP server:** `POST /mcp` (Streamable HTTP, JSON-RPC 2.0). `McpAuth` extracts a bearer from `Authorization` and compares with `ActiveSupport::SecurityUtils.secure_compare`; 401 renders a plain "MCP auth failed" page (Playwright target). See decision 0.8 for the OAuth fallback.
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.stderr:733:- **RSpec**, in the kickoff's priority order: token lifecycle with `travel_to` (25-minute refresh, 7-day expiry unaffected by refreshes, pause and catch-up, Mon/Tue escalation rule); sync jobs with fixture payloads (positions incl. removal, orders incl. cancel/replace and working stops, transactions incl. cash dividend, split, return of capital, CUSIP succession, fee items); journal linking (scale-in/out, orphan fill, sell-first legacy holding, bootstrap, ticker change on same CUSIP, R math); snapshot math (flows, late-landing deposit rebuild); MCP tool contracts (auth, each tool's schema and output, permission metadata excludes non-scheduled tools); scheduled runtime with a stubbed Messages API (turn cap, degraded mode).
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.stderr:734:- **VCR cassettes** in `spec/cassettes`, recorded against Schwab only once the app is Ready For Use, with a scrubber that replaces bearer tokens, refresh tokens, and account hash values before write. Until then, cassettes are hand-built from community-client response shapes and marked `# SCHWAB_SHAPE_UNVERIFIED`.
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.stderr:736:- **Playwright** (`e2e/`, `@playwright/test` via npm, the only Node dependency): dashboard in four banner states via a test-env-only `/playwright/scenarios/:name` reseed route, MCP 401 page, re-auth success and failure (FakeClient scripted), trade review flow.
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.stderr:759:8. MCP server + tool registry with permission metadata (after decision 0.8 is verified).
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.stderr:785:- Claude app custom connectors: static bearer header availability for this org (decision 0.8).
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.stderr:793:1. **PRD review with counselors** (`counselors run`, agents `codex-5.5-high` and `claude-fable`): the relevant PRD sections plus this plan's section for the step. Findings are folded into the plan before code.
